export const synthesis =
  'Chapter 13 assembles the ingredients developed earlier into a working first-principles calculation. The pseudopotential Kohn–Sham problem becomes a reciprocal-space total-energy and force problem coupled to a nonlinear density fixed point. Dielectric screening explains why the long-wavelength components of that fixed point can be numerically difficult and why preconditioning and mixing are physical as well as numerical ideas. PAW keeps the computational advantages of smooth functions while restoring atom-centered all-electron information through augmentation. Exact exchange adds a genuinely nonlocal Coulomb operator whose singular and long-range character requires special treatment in periodic plane-wave representations. Supercells then extend the same machinery to phonons, interfaces, surfaces, molecular dynamics, clusters, and molecules, at the price of explicit finite-size and electrostatic-boundary errors. With the plane-wave/grid route complete, Chapter 14 changes representation and asks how much of electronic structure can instead be understood from localized atom-centered orbitals.';
